In each group, the teams played three matches, one against each of the other teams. Victories were granted 3 points, while a draw was equal to 1 point. After completion of the group stage, the best two teams of each group advanced to the Round of 16 in the [[#Knockout stage|knockout stage]], in a way so all group winners started out meeting a runner-up from one of the other groups. This format was identical with the tournament structure being used in [[1998 FIFA World Cup|1998]]. A total of 64 games were played, including the [[#Final|final]] and a [[#Match for third place|match for third place]] between the two semi-final losers.

Group F was considered the [[group of death]] as it brought together Argentina, England, Nigeria and Sweden.<ref name="draw history"/>

The fixtures for the group stage were decided based on the draw results, as follows:

